# Agent Skills (Addy Osmani)

Before non-trivial technical work in this project:

1. Route via `.cursor/skills/using-agent-skills/SKILL.md`.
2. Read and follow the matching skill under `.cursor/skills/<name>/SKILL.md`.
3. Open linked files under `references/` when a skill points to them.
4. Prefer project skills over guessing; the user does not need to say "read skill" each time.

## Slash commands (explicit lifecycle)

When the user invokes these, follow the matching command skill (human-triggered):

| Command | Skill folder |
|---------|----------------|
| `/spec` | `.cursor/skills/spec/SKILL.md` |
| `/plan` | `.cursor/skills/plan/SKILL.md` |
| `/build` or `/build auto` | `.cursor/skills/build/SKILL.md` |
| `/test` | `.cursor/skills/test/SKILL.md` |
| `/review` | `.cursor/skills/review/SKILL.md` |
| `/code-simplify` | `.cursor/skills/code-simplify/SKILL.md` |
| `/ship` | `.cursor/skills/ship/SKILL.md` |
| `/webperf` | `.cursor/skills/webperf/SKILL.md` |
| `/log` | `.cursor/skills/log/SKILL.md` → `daily-work-record` |

## Artifacts

- Specs: `SPEC.md` (or `docs/SPEC.md`, `spec/`)
- Plans: `tasks/plan.md`, `tasks/todo.md`
- Worklog: `docs/worklog/YYYY-MM-DD.md`

Treat these as living documents while the work is in progress.

## Worklog

After a meaningful `/spec`, `/plan`, `/build`, `/review`, or `/ship` slice — or when the user is about to end the session — follow `.cursor/skills/daily-work-record/SKILL.md` and append today's entry (or remind the user to run `/log`). Do not invent progress.
